"""Authored event copy used by build_editorial_library.py.

All factual assertions are confined to the press desk's supplied event briefs.
The five longer columns are gazette, party, labour, business, and tabloid copy.
"""

EVENTS = {}

def add(event, heads, facts, angles, voices, judgments):
    assert len(heads) == len(facts) == len(angles) == len(judgments) == 3
    assert len(voices) == 5
    EVENTS[event] = dict(heads=heads, facts=facts, angles=angles, voices=voices, judgments=judgments)

add("POL_ELECTION_HELD",
    ["The colony has voted", "Ballots before the business of government", "An Assembly election enters the record"],
    ["An election to the Colonial Assembly has been held in {colony}.", "The colony has held its election to the Colonial Assembly.", "Voting in an election to the Colonial Assembly has taken place."],
    ["An election to the Colonial Assembly has been held in {colony}. The event places representation at the centre of public attention. The assessment of {target} should distinguish the holding of an election from any claim about what its result authorises.",
     "A ballot is a decision about representation, not a signed approval of every future measure. Following the election to the Colonial Assembly, that distinction deserves attention in any discussion of {target}. The colony has voted; political interpretation is a separate matter.",
     "The election to the Colonial Assembly belongs in the colony's public record. Its meaning should be considered without supplying results or promises that this report does not contain. For {target}, the event invites scrutiny of the relationship between representation and responsibility."],
    ["The gazette records the holding of the election without attributing a particular intention to the electorate. The act of voting and the subsequent exercise of public authority are distinct matters. An orderly account should preserve the difference between an electoral event and the interpretation placed upon it.",
     "Our movement regards representation as a duty, not a decoration to be worn until the next campaign. A ballot matters because political convictions should have a route into public decisions. Those who seek support ought to remember the purpose for which that support is sought.",
     "A working person's vote deserves the same respect as anyone else's. What matters to labour is whether representation takes wages, safe work and household needs seriously. An election gives those concerns a political setting; it does not make the work of defending them unnecessary.",
     "For owners and managers, an election is an institutional event before it is a forecast. A sound commercial judgment should not infer a tax measure, a spending plan or a business climate merely from the fact that voting has taken place. Decisions need their own evidence.",
     "The colony has had its say at the ballot box. That is a fine thing. It is also worth remembering that a vote is not a blank cheque. The people who do the representing should expect the people being represented to keep taking an interest."],
    ["This paper reserves judgment on {target}. Holding an election establishes that a contest occurred; it does not settle every question about the conduct or merits of those involved.",
     "In our view, {target} deserves criticism. A claim to public trust must withstand scrutiny after the ballots as well as before them; an election should never shelter inadequate political conduct.",
     "We regard {target} favourably in this assessment. Participation in representative politics deserves a fair hearing, and an election should be an occasion for reasoned judgment rather than reflexive hostility."])

add("POL_GOVERNMENT_FORMED",
    ["A new government takes shape", "Formation is the beginning of governing", "New ministry, practical obligations"],
    ["A new government has been formed in {colony}.", "The colony has a newly formed government.", "Government formation has produced a new administration in {colony}."],
    ["A new government has been formed in {colony}. Its formation establishes an administration; it does not establish the success of its future decisions. In considering {target}, the useful distinction is between assembling a government and meeting the obligations that come with governing.",
     "Government formation is a beginning. The new administration in {colony} gives public attention an institutional focus, while leaving its practical record to be made. Any judgment of {target} should recognise both the significance of formation and the limits of what formation alone can demonstrate.",
     "The colony has a new government. There is an obvious temptation to read a whole political future into that fact. A more useful approach to {target} begins with the administration that has actually been formed and the responsibilities inherent in exercising public authority."],
    ["The gazette records the new government's formation as a matter of public administration. An account of the change should avoid presuming either the contents of its programme or the outcome of its work. The existence of a ministry and the adequacy of its conduct require separate consideration.",
     "Our principles do not become less demanding when an administration is assembled. Government ought to be a means of advancing convictions through responsible action. The attraction of holding office is no substitute for an account of what office is for, and whose interests it should serve.",
     "Workers have good reason to ask what a government means for ordinary life. A list of officeholders cannot answer a question about safe work or a household budget. Labour's interest lies in the responsibilities that accompany power, and in keeping those responsibilities visible after formation.",
     "An administration is necessary machinery, but its formation is not itself an economic programme. Business readers should assess specific decisions when they exist rather than price in a collection of assumptions. Confidence should attach to competent conduct, not simply to the completion of a political arrangement.",
     "There is a new government. Now comes the difficult part of being one. A ministry can look splendid as an idea; people still have to live under its decisions. Keep the ceremonial satisfaction in proportion, and save some attention for what public office is supposed to accomplish."],
    ["The position of {target} should be assessed through the responsibilities of formation without a verdict on decisions not yet established by this report. A new government is a fact, not a forecast.",
     "We are unconvinced by {target}. The completion of an arrangement for office does not deserve to be mistaken for political merit; the public is entitled to a more demanding standard.",
     "We welcome the contribution of {target}. Forming an administration is a legitimate achievement, and it deserves recognition without requiring us to pretend that every future difficulty has already been solved."])

add("POL_NO_CONFIDENCE_PASSED",
    ["Assembly votes the government out", "Confidence withdrawn", "Office meets its parliamentary limit"],
    ["The Colonial Assembly has voted the government out in {colony}.", "The government has been voted out by the Colonial Assembly.", "An Assembly vote has removed the government in {colony}."],
    ["The Colonial Assembly has voted the government out. It is a decisive parliamentary event, though it does not by itself describe what follows. An assessment of {target} should start with the withdrawal of confidence and avoid announcing a successor that this report does not identify.",
     "A government cannot treat its relationship with the Assembly as a decorative part of office. The Assembly has voted the government out in {colony}. That outcome provides the immediate context for judging {target}, while leaving the merits of particular political alternatives to separate examination.",
     "The parliamentary right to withdraw confidence has produced a concrete result: the government has been voted out. Public attention now has a clear institutional fact to consider. For {target}, the issue is accountability under that result, rather than an imagined account of the negotiations surrounding it."],
    ["The gazette distinguishes the Assembly's decision from speculation concerning future administrative arrangements. The removal of a government is sufficient to warrant a clear entry in the public record. It should be described without attaching unreported causes, vote totals or subsequent appointments to the decision.",
     "Parliamentary responsibility must mean something when it is inconvenient as well as when it is useful. Our convictions require us to take the withdrawal of confidence seriously. Office is held within a representative system, and no political side should regard that system as merely an obstacle to itself.",
     "Workers cannot live on parliamentary drama, but they cannot afford to ignore who exercises public power. The removal of a government matters because authority carries obligations to ordinary people. Labour should judge the politics by those obligations rather than by the entertainment value of a defeat.",
     "A lost confidence vote is a political fact with administrative significance. It does not supply an economic forecast. Firms should distinguish the institutional decision from assumptions about contracts, taxes or spending; those subjects require specific information, however tempting it is to interpret everything through the parliamentary result.",
     "The government has been voted out. That is a result, not a hint. But a fall from office is not the same thing as an answer to every question in the colony. Enjoy the drama if you must; keep asking what responsible public life should look like."],
    ["The parliamentary outcome supplies the basis for scrutiny of {target}. This paper reports the loss of confidence without treating an unreported motive or future settlement as an established fact.",
     "Our assessment of {target} is adverse. Public authority deserves serious stewardship, and the parliamentary reckoning is an appropriate occasion to insist upon responsibility rather than excuses for inadequate political judgment.",
     "We take a sympathetic view of {target}. A parliamentary defeat is decisive for office, but it need not be treated as a final moral verdict on every person or position involved."])

add("POL_NO_CONFIDENCE_FAILED",
    ["Bid to remove government fails", "Confidence challenge falls short", "Government survives the Assembly test"],
    ["A vote to bring down the government has failed in {colony}.", "The attempt to remove the government by an Assembly vote has failed.", "The government has survived a vote intended to bring it down."],
    ["The vote to bring down the government has failed. The result settles that attempt, not every argument about the administration. For {target}, it is important to distinguish survival of a parliamentary challenge from an unlimited endorsement of political conduct or future decisions.",
     "Remaining in office and winning every argument are different achievements. The government's opponents have failed to bring it down by a vote in the Assembly. This is the institutional fact against which the conduct of {target} should be considered, without inventing a margin or motive.",
     "The Assembly challenge has not removed the government. A failed vote is a definite parliamentary outcome, even where the wider political argument remains open. The question for readers considering {target} is what responsible conduct requires after this attempt, rather than what an imagined tally might suggest."],
    ["The gazette records that the attempt to bring down the administration was unsuccessful. The outcome should not be enlarged into a statement about the Assembly's view of every governmental measure. Confidence proceedings have a defined object, and a reliable account should remain attentive to that object.",
     "A parliamentary tactic should serve political principles, not replace them. Our movement ought to judge both government and opposition by the case each makes for the public good. Surviving a challenge does not erase that obligation, and losing one does not relieve anyone of the need for convictions.",
     "There are people whose whole interest in this vote is whether it helps them live decently. That is a sensible standard. Labour should keep work, wages and safety in view when assessing the politics, rather than allowing the survival of a ministry to become an end in itself.",
     "The vote's failure establishes an institutional outcome. It cannot establish that economic conditions are sound or that future policy will be predictable. Commercial readers should resist turning a parliamentary survival into a general assurance about matters for which a confidence vote supplies no direct evidence.",
     "The attempt failed. The government was not brought down. Put away the imaginary resignation speech, but do not put away the questions. Holding on to office is something politicians care about a great deal. Readers are allowed to care just as much about what office is used for."],
    ["The role of {target} merits examination on the known outcome. A failed removal attempt should be reported clearly, without supplying an unreported political bargain as its explanation.",
     "We find the conduct of {target} wanting. Whatever the result of this attempt, parliamentary manoeuvre is no substitute for political responsibility or an adequate account of the public interest.",
     "We favour {target} in this assessment. A political position deserves to be judged on its merits, and the failed challenge offers no warrant for treating hostile assumptions as proven conclusions."])

add("POL_SCANDAL_REVEALED",
    ["Party leader faces a public scandal", "Leadership under an unwelcome spotlight", "A scandal tests political trust"],
    ["A scandal concerning a party leader has come to light in {colony}.", "A party leader is the subject of a newly revealed scandal.", "A scandal about a party leader has become public in the colony."],
    ["A scandal about a party leader has come to light. The revelation makes political trust an immediate subject of public attention. An assessment of {target} must distinguish that known fact from unreported details about the conduct involved, its cause or any proceedings that might follow.",
     "Leadership brings a claim to trust. A newly revealed scandal concerning a party leader gives that claim an uncomfortable setting in {colony}. Readers considering {target} should be able to examine responsibility without being invited to accept a more specific accusation than the report establishes.",
     "The public record now includes a scandal about a party leader. That is serious political news; it is not permission to fill gaps with an attractive story. For {target}, the question of trust deserves attention without a fabricated account of money, private life or criminal conduct."],
    ["The gazette confines its factual account to the revelation of the scandal. A political embarrassment and a finding under law are distinct matters. The public record is best served by keeping the distinction clear and by avoiding particulars which have not been supplied to this newspaper.",
     "Our political principles ought to survive the discomfort of applying them to leaders. Trust is not a private asset belonging to a party hierarchy. It concerns the people asked to give their support, and they deserve an argument about responsibility that does not depend on convenient invention.",
     "Workers know the difference between being held responsible and being made the subject of gossip. Political leaders should face a serious standard, with fair treatment included in it. Labour's concern is public trust and the use of authority, not the pleasure of seeing a prominent name embarrassed.",
     "Reputation matters, but sound judgment requires more than a scandal label. A commercial assessment should avoid inferring a financial loss, a regulatory consequence or an administrative change that has not been established. Confidence should rest on a careful account, particularly when political controversy encourages hasty conclusions.",
     "A leader, a scandal, and a story everyone can be tempted to improve in the telling. Resist the temptation. The revelation is news enough. Readers deserve a sharp question about trust, not a collection of invented details dressed up as the delicious part of the story."],
    ["This paper treats {target} as a subject for scrutiny, while withholding conclusions the reported revelation does not establish. Attention to trust need not depend upon an invented account of wrongdoing.",
     "In our judgment, {target} does not deserve confidence in this matter. Political trust requires a demanding standard, and the scandal is an appropriate occasion for a distinctly critical assessment.",
     "We consider {target} unfairly served by a rush to condemnation. A scandal's existence is not a complete account of responsibility, and a fair hearing remains worth defending even in unwelcome publicity."])

add("POL_PARTNER_LEFT",
    ["Party walks out of government", "A governing partnership breaks", "Departure redraws the question of cooperation"],
    ["A party has walked out of the government in {colony}.", "A governing party has left the colony's government.", "The government has lost a party from its governing arrangement."],
    ["A party has walked out of the government in {colony}. The departure is a change in the governing arrangement, not a complete account of its consequences. In considering {target}, readers should distinguish the fact of leaving from assumptions about parliamentary strength or a successor ministry.",
     "Cooperation in government has reached a break: a party has walked out. The event raises the question of what parties owe an arrangement they enter. For {target}, responsibility should be considered without pretending that the report supplies the departing party's reasons or the administration's next steps.",
     "Leaving a government is a political act with institutional significance. A party has taken that step in {colony}. Its effect on the governing relationship is the subject of this report; judgments of {target} should not depend on an invented dispute, ultimatum or distribution of seats."],
    ["The gazette records the departure without presuming that the government itself has fallen. A change in its composition and the end of an administration are different propositions. Administrative clarity requires attention to what has occurred rather than an account of arrangements not established by the departure alone.",
     "There is a principled question beneath every argument about staying in office: what makes cooperation worth sustaining? Our movement should answer it honestly. Neither loyalty to an arrangement nor departure from it is automatically virtuous; each must be judged against the political commitments it is meant to serve.",
     "Working people need more from parties than a performance of falling out. Cooperation matters when it helps secure a decent life; a break deserves scrutiny for the same reason. Labour should ask whose needs are being defended, without allowing claims about those needs to stand in for evidence.",
     "A party's departure is a change in the political arrangement. It is not proof that contracts will be disrupted or that policy will reverse. Owners and managers should keep their assessments tied to identifiable decisions rather than treating every break in political cooperation as an economic forecast.",
     "A party has left the government. That much is plain. The temptation is to write the row, the slammed door and the perfect final insult. None of that is needed. A partnership has broken; the colony is entitled to ask what responsible politics looks like after a break."],
    ["The conduct of {target} should be examined in the light of the departure itself. This paper does not attribute an unreported motive to the break or announce an unreported governmental outcome.",
     "We take a critical view of {target}. Governing relationships require serious political judgment, and a break in cooperation is an appropriate moment to question whether that standard has been met.",
     "We support {target} in this assessment. Cooperation is not an obligation to accept every political arrangement indefinitely; a fair judgment must leave room for a principled position when relationships change."])

add("POL_LEADER_CHANGED",
    ["Party names a new leader", "Leadership changes hands", "A new name at the head of the party"],
    ["A party has a new leader in {colony}.", "Leadership of a political party has changed in the colony.", "A new leader is now at the head of a party in {colony}."],
    ["A party has a new leader in {colony}. A change at the head of an organisation is a political fact; a change in its programme is a separate question. Readers considering {target} should not have to accept the second as a necessary consequence of the first.",
     "The name at the head of a party has changed. The event invites attention to what leadership means, beyond the identity of the person holding it. In assessing {target}, the useful question concerns responsibility for a political organisation rather than an invented personal history.",
     "New leadership gives a party a different person to answer for its public direction. That is the established development in {colony}. Any assessment of {target} should leave unreported policies, internal vote totals and explanations for the change outside the factual account of the event."],
    ["The gazette records the change of party leadership without presuming the circumstances in which it occurred. The replacement of a leader does not establish a resignation, a dismissal or an internal contest unless those particulars are separately known. A precise notice should avoid supplying them by implication.",
     "A party's principles should not be reduced to the personality at its head. Our movement believes leadership is a responsibility to carry convictions into public life. A new name deserves attention, but the enduring question is whether political organisation serves something beyond the advancement of its most visible member.",
     "Labour has reason to pay attention to a new party leader, without assuming that a different face means a different life for workers. Wages, safety and household needs remain the useful yardstick. A political organisation should be judged by how seriously it takes those matters, whoever speaks for it.",
     "Management readers understand that a change in leadership is not a complete strategy document. The same restraint is useful in politics. A new party head does not establish a tax proposal or an economic policy, and decisions should not be anticipated as facts merely because the spokesperson has changed.",
     "New leader. Same need to ask questions. A fresh name can make a political organisation look like a new story, but readers need more than a portrait to judge it. Keep the attention on responsibility; a personality is a person, not a programme for the whole colony."],
    ["This paper approaches {target} without a verdict supplied by the fact of replacement. Leadership has changed; the merits of conduct and proposals require their own assessment on an adequate record.",
     "We are not persuaded by {target}. A change of leadership should not be allowed to turn political scrutiny into a courtesy exercise; public trust requires more than a place at the head of a party.",
     "We welcome {target} in this assessment. New leadership deserves the opportunity for a fair hearing, and recognition of that opportunity need not depend on inventing achievements before they occur."])

add("POL_LEADERSHIP_RACE_OPENED",
    ["Party leader faces a challenge", "Leadership becomes a contested question", "A challenge inside the party"],
    ["A party's leader is being challenged in {colony}.", "A challenge to a party leader has opened in the colony.", "The leadership of a political party is under challenge."],
    ["A party's leader is being challenged in {colony}. The challenge places authority within the organisation in question, without deciding who should exercise it. Readers assessing {target} should distinguish the opening of a contest from an outcome that has not been established by this report.",
     "The right to lead a party is being contested. That is the political development, rather than proof of an eventual removal or victory. An examination of {target} should begin with the challenge itself and leave the candidates' unreported programmes outside the factual account.",
     "Leadership can appear settled until it becomes a question again. A party leader now faces a challenge in {colony}. For {target}, the relevant issue is the exercise and scrutiny of political authority, not an imagined story about who has already secured the organisation's support."],
    ["The gazette notes the challenge as an internal political development. It records neither a change of leader nor the result of any contest. A reliable account should retain that distinction, particularly where a challenge encourages speculation about outcomes before the organisation has an established decision to report.",
     "A party ought to be capable of discussing its direction without treating every question as disloyalty. Our principles also require a contest to be about more than personal advancement. The purpose of challenging leadership should be intelligible in terms of the convictions an organisation exists to serve.",
     "An argument over leadership deserves workers' attention when it concerns whose needs a party represents. It deserves rather less admiration as a quarrel over a title. Labour should keep asking about work and daily life, rather than choosing a side on the strength of an internal contest alone.",
     "A leadership challenge can attract considerable political attention without establishing any change in policy. Business readers should separate an internal question of authority from an economic decision. The possibility of a new spokesperson is not evidence of a specific future rule, commitment or commercial condition for the colony.",
     "There is a challenge to a party leader. Plenty of room for excitement; no room to print a winner who has not been established. Readers can follow the contest without being sold a finished story. The title matters, but what someone wants to do with it matters more."],
    ["The position of {target} deserves scrutiny without assuming that a challenge is either justified or doomed. The existence of a contest is the known fact on which this account rests.",
     "Our assessment of {target} is critical. Political leadership should withstand serious questioning, and an internal challenge is no reason to suspend the demanding standards that public responsibility properly requires.",
     "We take a favourable view of {target}. A leadership challenge does not make hostile interpretations correct, and a political position deserves support where the case against it rests on assumption."])

add("POL_PARTY_SPLIT",
    ["Party divides in two", "A political organisation breaks apart", "Unity gives way to a party split"],
    ["A political party has split in two in {colony}.", "The colony has seen a party divide into two organisations.", "A split has divided a political party in the colony."],
    ["A political party has split in two in {colony}. The division is an organisational fact, not a complete explanation of the differences behind it. In considering {target}, readers should distinguish the break itself from unreported motives, ideological labels or claims about the balance of parliamentary strength.",
     "Party unity has given way to division. A party has split in two, making political organisation itself the subject of the news. The assessment of {target} should address that break without treating either part as the natural owner of principles this report does not specify.",
     "A split has produced two parts where a party previously stood together. That is the development established in {colony}. Readers considering {target} should not be asked to accept an invented account of the dispute or an electoral forecast as part of the factual report."],
    ["The gazette records the division of the party without ascribing a particular doctrine or dispute to either part. Organisational separation is distinct from a transfer of public office or a change of government. The report should therefore remain precise about the development that has actually been established.",
     "Political unity has value when it enables common convictions to act. It is not a principle that can settle every disagreement by itself. Our movement should judge a division by the commitments at stake, rather than granting either unity or separation an automatic claim to righteousness in every case.",
     "Workers deserve political organisations that take their interests seriously, whether those organisations stand together or apart. A split should be judged with that purpose in mind. Labour gains little from celebrating an internal victory if the question of a decent working life disappears behind the competing party labels.",
     "An organisational division in politics is not the same as a change in the rules under which firms operate. Commercial readers should avoid treating the split as a ready-made forecast. Representation and future decisions require examination in their own right, without an assumed programme attached to either part.",
     "A party has split in two. A simple sentence for a very public break. There is no need to invent the private quarrel to make it interesting. Readers should ask what the division is for, and whether the people being represented will find something more useful than competing claims to loyalty."],
    ["The responsibility of {target} should be considered without presuming the split's cause or its eventual consequences. This account records an organisational division and reserves judgment on particulars not supplied.",
     "We judge {target} harshly in this matter. Political organisation carries obligations beyond the comfort of its leaders, and division is an appropriate occasion to question the quality of that stewardship.",
     "We support {target} in this assessment. Unity is not an unlimited obligation, and a fair political judgment must allow that separation can deserve defence rather than automatic condemnation for breaking ranks."])

add("POL_BILL_DEFEATED",
    ["Assembly votes down government bill", "A proposal meets its parliamentary limit", "Government legislation fails the vote"],
    ["A government bill has been voted down in the Colonial Assembly.", "The Assembly has rejected a bill put forward by the government.", "A proposed government bill has failed in the Assembly vote."],
    ["A government bill has been voted down in the Colonial Assembly. The result concerns the proposal put to the vote; it should not be enlarged into an unreported change of government. In assessing {target}, readers should distinguish legislative defeat from a complete account of political authority.",
     "Proposing legislation does not ensure its passage. The Assembly has voted down a government bill in {colony}. That outcome gives a concrete setting to scrutiny of {target}, without supplying the bill's provisions, the voting margin or the reasons members had for rejecting it.",
     "The government's bill has not passed the Assembly. It is a definite result for the proposed legislation, even without a detailed account of the measure. Any judgment of {target} should therefore address the political handling of a rejected proposal without inventing what the proposal would have done."],
    ["The gazette records the defeat of the bill as a legislative event. A rejection and a statutory change are different things, and the former should not be described as though the latter had occurred. An orderly public account also avoids presuming that the vote had an unreported constitutional consequence.",
     "A legislature is supposed to decide, not merely to decorate a government's intentions. Our principles require us to take a rejected measure seriously without assuming that every rejection is wise. The merits of a political proposal belong in the argument; possession of office cannot settle them on its own.",
     "For workers, the point of a law is what it means in daily life. A defeated bill cannot be assessed through invented benefits or harms. Labour should demand clear political responsibility while remembering that a vote on a proposal and the practical conditions of work are distinct matters.",
     "A bill that has been rejected is not a new operating rule. Business readers should resist the temptation to treat the proposal as enacted, or the defeat as a promise about all future legislation. Commercial planning needs the actual legal position, with proposed changes distinguished from decisions that take effect.",
     "The government wanted a bill through. The Assembly voted it down. That is a story without an invented row, a secret bargain or a dramatic resignation. A proposal has hit the parliamentary wall. Readers can ask who handled it well without pretending to know provisions that have not been reported."],
    ["The conduct of {target} warrants examination against the rejected proposal. This paper records the legislative result without adopting an unreported explanation for it or declaring a wider political outcome.",
     "We take an adverse view of {target}. Serious legislative work requires judgment as well as intention, and a defeated proposal is a proper occasion to question whether that responsibility has been met.",
     "We defend {target} against an easy adverse verdict. A parliamentary defeat does not by itself settle the merits of a political position, and a rejected proposal can still deserve a fair hearing."])

add("HOME_DEMAND_RAISED",
    ["Home world raises its demands", "A larger claim on the colony", "Distant authority asks for more"],
    ["The home world has raised what it demands of the colony.", "The demands placed on the colony by the home world have increased.", "The home world is demanding more from {colony}."],
    ["The home world has raised what it demands of the colony. The increase puts the relationship between distant authority and local obligation in focus. Readers considering {target} should distinguish the higher demand from any unreported account of its size, form or practical enforcement.",
     "A demand made at a distance still concerns the people expected to meet it. The home world is asking more of {colony}. In assessing {target}, the question is how authority and obligation should be judged, without assuming the particular terms that this report does not supply.",
     "The colony faces increased demands from the home world. That change is the news; the extent of its burden is not specified here. A fair account of {target} should examine the relationship it represents without fabricating a quantity, a deadline or a reason for the increase."],
    ["The gazette notes the increase as a change in the demands placed upon the colony. The existence of a higher requirement should be kept distinct from any assumption about its particulars. An administrative account is most useful when it describes the known obligation without supplying terms not established by the notice.",
     "Our politics begins from the conviction that authority should answer a serious question about legitimacy. Distance does not remove that question. A larger demand deserves examination in terms of what the colony owes and what its people can justly be asked to bear, rather than submission to a grand title.",
     "When more is demanded of a colony, working people have reason to ask who is expected to carry the burden. The question should be asked without pretending the answer is already known. Labour's concern is fair treatment for the people whose work supports the common undertaking.",
     "An increased demand is a claim on the colony, not a sufficiently detailed entry for a business forecast. Managers should distinguish its existence from assumptions about the resources involved. A reasoned assessment requires the actual terms before attaching a cost or a commercial consequence to the change.",
     "More. It is a short word when somebody else has to supply it. The home world has increased its demands on the colony. Readers deserve a plain question about fairness, without being sold a made-up bill or a promise about how easy it will be to meet."],
    ["This paper examines {target} through the increased demand, without presuming either its justification or its practical burden. The change is established; its unreported terms should remain outside the factual account.",
     "We regard {target} critically. A higher demand deserves more than automatic deference, and authority should not be excused from defending the fairness of what it asks other people to bear.",
     "We support {target} in this assessment. An increased demand is not automatically an unjust one, and a responsible judgment should allow a fair case rather than beginning with a verdict of bad faith."])

add("HOME_SANCTION",
    ["Home world punishes the colony", "A sanction enters the colonial relationship", "Authority takes a punitive turn"],
    ["The home world has punished the colony.", "A punishment has been imposed on {colony} by the home world.", "The colony is the subject of punitive action by the home world."],
    ["The home world has punished the colony. The action establishes a punitive development in the relationship, not the particular effects of that action. Scrutiny of {target} should address the use of authority without adding an unreported restriction, financial loss or change in supplies to the account.",
     "Punishment is a claim that authority may impose a consequence on others. The home world has exercised that claim against {colony}. In considering {target}, readers should be able to examine fairness and responsibility without being asked to accept an invented explanation of the dispute.",
     "A punitive action by the home world now forms part of the colony's affairs. The report establishes that punishment occurred, while leaving its particulars unstated. Any assessment of {target} should therefore distinguish the political judgment of the action from assertions about consequences not supplied here."],
    ["The gazette records the punishment without assigning a particular form to it. A punitive action should be described with due care, since assumptions about its terms could misstate the colony's position. The public interest is served by keeping the known action separate from an inferred account of its operation.",
     "Our principles require scrutiny of power when it punishes, not only when it makes promises. The relationship between the colony and the home world cannot be reduced to the prestige of the authority involved. A political argument should explain why a consequence is just, rather than treating power as its own justification.",
     "Workers should not disappear from the discussion when authorities exchange claims about punishment. Fairness includes attention to ordinary people who may have no voice in those claims. Labour must ask who should bear responsibility, while avoiding an invented account of the burden actually imposed by this action.",
     "Punitive action deserves a careful commercial assessment, but its existence does not identify a cost. Owners and managers should not presume a particular restriction on trade, finance or materials from the label alone. The sensible approach is to distinguish the political event from its still unspecified operating terms.",
     "The home world has punished the colony. A serious sentence, and a reason to ask serious questions. What makes a punishment fair? Who deserves to answer for it? Those are legitimate questions. A dramatic story about shortages or losses would need facts this report does not contain."],
    ["The position of {target} should be assessed without supplying an unreported offence or penalty. This paper records the punitive action while reserving judgment on particulars not established in the report.",
     "We criticise {target} in this matter. The exercise or handling of punitive authority requires a more demanding standard than the fact of power, and we find the political stewardship wanting.",
     "We take a sympathetic view of {target}. The fact of punishment does not prove every hostile interpretation, and the question of responsibility deserves a fair hearing rather than an automatic condemnation."])

add("HOME_EXPEDITION_SENT",
    ["Home world sends punitive expedition", "An expedition with a punitive purpose", "Distant authority dispatches an expedition"],
    ["The home world has sent a punitive expedition.", "A punitive expedition has been dispatched by the home world.", "The home world has dispatched an expedition intended to punish the colony."],
    ["The home world has sent a punitive expedition. Dispatch and arrival are different events, and this report establishes only the former. Readers considering {target} should not be asked to accept an invented landing, confrontation or account of force as part of the news of its departure.",
     "A punitive expedition has been dispatched by the home world. Its stated purpose makes the action a serious question of authority and responsibility. For {target}, scrutiny should begin with the dispatch itself, without supplying a route, a timetable or a result that the report does not establish.",
     "The relationship with the home world now includes the dispatch of an expedition intended to punish the colony. That is a substantial political event on its own. An assessment of {target} should preserve the distinction between what has been sent and what has actually happened in {colony}."],
    ["The gazette records the dispatch without anticipating subsequent events. A precise account should not describe the expedition as present in the colony or attribute an encounter to it. The punitive purpose is established, while composition, timing and any eventual action remain outside the particulars supplied to this notice.",
     "A claim to authority becomes especially important to examine when it takes a punitive form. Our convictions require attention to legitimacy and responsibility, without turning that political argument into an invented battle. The colony deserves a case about power that can be made without adding events to the record.",
     "Ordinary people should remain visible in arguments about distant power. Labour's concern is the right to live and work without being treated as scenery for somebody else's assertion of authority. That concern is strong enough without claims about casualties, damage or disruption that have not been established.",
     "Dispatch of an expedition is not a complete account of conditions in the colony. Commercial readers should resist translating it automatically into a forecast of interruptions or losses. A careful judgment separates the known political action from assumptions about timing, physical effects and the terms of any eventual encounter.",
     "Sent does not mean arrived. Remember that before the imagination supplies a scene at the port. The home world has dispatched a punitive expedition. The purpose is serious enough to deserve attention without a fictional confrontation. Readers need clear questions about authority, not a battle that exists only in the telling."],
    ["The conduct of {target} warrants scrutiny in relation to the dispatch. This newspaper does not treat the expedition's purpose as evidence of an unreported encounter or an established outcome in the colony.",
     "We judge {target} adversely. Punitive power demands an exacting political standard, and the dispatch is an appropriate occasion to question the quality and fairness of the responsibility being exercised.",
     "We defend {target} against a verdict based on imagined events. The expedition's dispatch is serious news, but a fair assessment must not convert every feared consequence into an accusation already proven."])

add("HOME_PETITION_ANSWERED",
    ["Home world answers colony's petition", "A reply to the colonial petition", "Petition receives an answer"],
    ["The home world has answered the colony's petition.", "A reply to the colony's petition has come from the home world.", "The colony has received an answer to its petition from the home world."],
    ["The home world has answered the colony's petition. A response is established, but the fact of a reply does not itself say whether the colony's request was granted. Readers considering {target} should keep that distinction clear rather than treating an answer as an automatic concession.",
     "A petition is a request to authority; an answer is not necessarily the response its authors sought. The home world has replied to the colony's petition. An assessment of {target} should begin with that known exchange, without supplying favourable or adverse terms absent from this account.",
     "The colonial petition has an answer from the home world. That gives the relationship a recorded response, not a warrant to invent its contents. For {target}, the question is responsible handling of a petition and its reply, rather than a victory or defeat presumed from the word 'answered'."],
    ["The gazette records the reply while distinguishing receipt of an answer from the substance of a decision. A petition's disposition should not be inferred from the existence of correspondence alone. Public understanding is best served by avoiding a description of terms not contained in the particulars of this notice.",
     "Our movement takes seriously the colony's right to make its case. It should take equally seriously the difference between being answered and being satisfied. A principled politics needs more than the appearance of consultation; it needs an argument about what authority owes to people who petition it.",
     "For labour, the value of a petition lies in the needs it is meant to express. A reply should be judged with those needs in mind. Workers should not be asked to celebrate the existence of an answer as though correspondence alone established a practical improvement in daily life.",
     "A reply is information, but its existence is not a financial or operational commitment. Business readers should avoid inferring a concession, a new capacity or a changed obligation from the fact that a petition has been answered. The terms of an answer matter more than the completion of an exchange.",
     "An answer has come. That is news. Whether it is the answer the colony wanted is a different question. Do not let a tidy word do the work of a missing explanation. Readers deserve the difference between getting a reply and getting what was asked for."],
    ["The role of {target} should be considered without assuming the reply's terms. This paper records the answer as an established event and leaves unreported acceptance or refusal outside its factual account.",
     "We find {target} unconvincing in this matter. A petition deserves responsible political handling, and the existence of an answer is insufficient reason to suspend scrutiny or congratulate inadequate stewardship.",
     "We support {target} in this assessment. Seeking and handling a response deserves a fair hearing; an answer should not become the occasion for hostile conclusions founded on terms this account does not establish."])

add("HOME_SHIP_BUILT",
    ["Shipbuilding for the colony route", "Home world builds for the colonial crossing", "Route gains a shipbuilding development"],
    ["The home world has built a larger ship or an additional ship for the colony route.", "Shipbuilding by the home world has provided a larger vessel or another vessel for the colony route.", "A larger ship or one more ship has been built for the colony route."],
    ["The home world has built a larger ship or an additional ship for the colony route. The construction is a transport development, not an announcement of arrival. In assessing {target}, readers should distinguish provision of a vessel from an unreported schedule, cargo or immediate change in supplies.",
     "A ship built for the colony route is a physical commitment to that connection. The home world has provided a larger vessel or another vessel. For {target}, the event invites judgment about transport provision without assuming that construction establishes a particular sailing date or frequency of service.",
     "The route to the colony is the subject of a shipbuilding development: the home world has built a larger ship or one more ship. Any assessment of {target} should begin there, rather than with a forecast of passengers or goods that the report does not supply."],
    ["The gazette records the construction for the colonial route without describing the vessel as having reached the colony. Completion of a ship and completion of a voyage are distinct administrative facts. A useful notice should also avoid assigning an unreported cargo capacity or timetable to the development.",
     "Transport is part of the material relationship between the colony and the home world. Our principles require attention to how that relationship serves people, not simply admiration for a vessel. The political question is what responsible provision means, and it cannot be settled by inventing a promised benefit.",
     "Ships matter to working people because a distant connection is part of the colony's common life. That does not make every claim about a new vessel true. Labour should ask how transport serves ordinary needs, without treating construction as proof of cheaper goods or a better household budget.",
     "A larger vessel or an additional vessel should not be confused with an established volume of delivered freight. Commercial planning requires the distinction between physical provision and actual service. Managers should avoid converting this shipbuilding report into a precise change in supply, cost or delivery dates without the necessary particulars.",
     "A ship has been built for the route. Good material for a grand picture of the future; less useful as proof of what is on a shop shelf today. Keep the distinction clear. Building a vessel and watching it arrive are different stories, however attractive it is to combine them."],
    ["The contribution of {target} should be assessed through the reported construction, without assuming an unreported improvement in service. This account establishes a vessel development, not the full terms of future voyages.",
     "We remain critical of {target}. A shipbuilding development should not place transport stewardship beyond scrutiny; the colony deserves a demanding standard rather than automatic admiration for the announcement of a vessel.",
     "We welcome {target} in this assessment. Construction for the route deserves recognition as a tangible development, even while a fair account keeps that achievement distinct from promises about voyages not established here."])

add("HOME_SHIPPING_REFUSED",
    ["Request for more shipping refused", "Home world declines route expansion request", "No assent to the colony's shipping plea"],
    ["The home world has refused the colony's request for more shipping.", "A colonial request for additional shipping has been rejected by the home world.", "The colony's plea for more shipping has been refused."],
    ["The home world has refused the colony's request for more shipping. The refusal concerns an increase, not an established withdrawal of existing service. Readers judging {target} should keep that limit in view, without supplying a change in voyages or capacity that the report does not identify.",
     "More shipping was requested; the home world has refused. That is the result of the colonial request, rather than a complete account of the route's future. Scrutiny of {target} should examine the handling of the request without inventing either the reasons for refusal or a resulting shortage.",
     "The colony's request for additional shipping has not been accepted by the home world. A refusal is a concrete decision, even without its detailed explanation. For {target}, the relevant question is responsibility in the transport relationship, not a presumed cancellation of service already in place."],
    ["The gazette records rejection of the request for an increase. It should not be read as notice that existing shipping has ceased. A sound administrative account preserves the distinction between declining a proposed addition and altering an established arrangement, unless the latter is separately supported by the record.",
     "The colony's claim to a fair hearing should not depend upon whether a request is convenient to distant authority. Our principles require a serious argument about the relationship, including the right to question a refusal. That argument should be made without adding a motive the report does not establish.",
     "Transport concerns belong in labour's politics because ordinary life depends on the colony's material arrangements. A refused request deserves attention to whose needs are being heard. Workers gain nothing from an invented promise, but they also need not treat refusal as something too distant or grand to question.",
     "A rejected increase should not be entered into a forecast as a reduction in current service. Business readers need that distinction. The refusal establishes the outcome of a request; it does not identify its reasons or specify a change in delivered volumes, prices or the schedule of existing voyages.",
     "The answer to more shipping is no. That is disappointing material for anyone who likes an easy story of endless improvement. It is still not a story about ships being cancelled. Readers can judge a refusal sharply without being given a more dramatic event than the one that happened."],
    ["The responsibility of {target} should be examined through the refused request. This paper does not presume an explanation for the refusal or a change in existing shipping that has not been reported.",
     "We criticise {target} over the handling of this matter. A colony's transport needs deserve serious political stewardship, and a refusal should prompt scrutiny rather than an effortless acceptance of the outcome.",
     "We defend {target} against an automatic adverse judgment. Refusal of a request does not establish every claim about its merits, and fair assessment requires more than disappointment with the answer."])

add("LAW_CHARTER_AMENDED",
    ["Home world changes the charter", "Colonial charter amended", "The terms of authority are altered"],
    ["The home world has changed the colony's charter.", "An amendment to the colony's charter has been made by the home world.", "The colony's charter has been altered by the home world."],
    ["The home world has changed the colony's charter. A change to the governing framework deserves a precise account, not a guess at the powers affected. In considering {target}, readers should distinguish the fact of amendment from any particular new permission or restriction not specified in this report.",
     "The terms under which the colony is governed have a recorded amendment: the home world has changed the charter. For {target}, the event invites scrutiny of authority and legitimacy. It does not license an invented account of which local decisions have become lawful or unlawful.",
     "A charter amendment has been made by the home world. The change belongs to the colony's legal framework, while its detailed operation is a separate matter. Readers judging {target} should be able to discuss the use of authority without accepting unspecified legal consequences as established facts."],
    ["The gazette records the amendment while avoiding an account of provisions not supplied here. A constitutional instrument and the administrative acts made under it are distinct matters. Public understanding requires accurate terms, and precision is especially necessary where a change in the charter invites broad assumptions about local power.",
     "Our movement believes the rules of public authority deserve political argument, not ceremonial submission. A charter shapes the relationship between the colony and the home world. The question of legitimacy should therefore remain visible, without pretending that a general principle tells us the exact content of this particular amendment.",
     "Workers have a stake in the framework within which political choices are made. A charter should not be treated as too distant a subject for ordinary people. Labour must ask how authority is justified and whose voice counts, while leaving unreported changes to specific rights outside the factual account.",
     "A charter amendment warrants attention, but it is not a sufficiently detailed basis for changing an operating assumption. Owners and managers should distinguish the known alteration of the framework from particular legal effects. Commercial judgment requires the relevant provision, rather than a general impression that the rules have changed.",
     "The charter has changed. It may sound like a subject for a very long document, and it is still a subject for the people who live under it. Ask about authority. Ask about fairness. Do not accept a made-up list of new powers just because the word 'charter' sounds impressive."],
    ["This paper examines {target} through the fact of the amendment, without announcing a specific legal effect not contained in the report. The exercise of authority and its justification merit separate scrutiny.",
     "We take a critical view of {target}. Altering the governing framework calls for exacting political responsibility, and the prestige of a charter supplies no automatic defence against questions about that responsibility.",
     "We support {target} in this assessment. A charter change deserves judgment on its merits, rather than condemnation merely because the framework has been altered by an authority exercising its claimed role."])

add("LAW_CHARTER_DEFIANCE",
    ["Colony openly defies its charter", "A public break with charter authority", "Charter compliance becomes an open dispute"],
    ["The colony is openly defying its charter.", "Open defiance of the charter is taking place in {colony}.", "The colony has taken an openly defiant position towards its charter."],
    ["The colony is openly defying its charter. The defiance is established; a particular punishment or response is not. An assessment of {target} should distinguish the political and legal question posed by that stance from an invented account of what the home world has done in reply.",
     "The relationship between local action and charter authority is an open question of defiance in {colony}. That is the development reported here. Readers considering {target} should be able to judge responsibility without accepting an unreported sanction, demand or confrontation as part of the event.",
     "Charter authority is being openly defied by the colony. The stance deserves serious attention in its own right. For {target}, the question is how to judge an explicit refusal of compliance, without presuming the precise act involved or treating a possible consequence as already established."],
    ["The gazette records the defiance without assuming an amendment to the charter. Acting against a framework and changing that framework are distinct matters. A precise account should also separate the colony's position from any subsequent action by the home world, which this report does not establish as having occurred.",
     "Political principle is tested when obedience and conviction are said to pull apart. Our movement should be able to explain its judgment of authority rather than treating either compliance or defiance as automatically virtuous. A serious argument concerns legitimacy and responsibility, not the appeal of a defiant gesture alone.",
     "Working people deserve a voice in arguments about the authority under which they live. They also deserve to be kept in view when political gestures are admired. Labour should ask whose interests a position serves without inventing either the cost of defiance or a promised improvement in daily life.",
     "Open charter defiance is a legal and political fact, not a complete statement of operating consequences. Business readers should avoid assuming that a sanction has followed or that an established rule has simply ceased to exist. Assessment requires a distinction between the stance taken and the response actually reported.",
     "The colony is openly defying its charter. A big gesture, a serious question. But do not write the punishment into the story before it has been established. Readers can ask whether defiance is brave, reckless or justified without being sold a confrontation that belongs to somebody's imagination."],
    ["The position of {target} warrants scrutiny through the reported defiance. This account does not presume the precise breach or announce a punitive consequence that has not been established in the report.",
     "We judge {target} adversely. Defiance demands a serious account of responsibility, and a bold stance should not be allowed to shelter inadequate political judgment behind the attraction of its own gesture.",
     "We defend {target} in this assessment. Compliance is not the only possible political virtue, and a fair hearing must allow a principled challenge to authority rather than treating defiance as self-proving guilt."])

add("UNION_STRIKE_CALLED",
    ["Union calls a strike", "A call to withhold labour", "Work becomes the subject of a strike call"],
    ["A union has called a strike in {colony}.", "A strike has been called by a union in the colony.", "The colony has a union call for strike action."],
    ["A union has called a strike in {colony}. The call establishes a labour action, not an account of its participation or outcome. Readers considering {target} should distinguish the decision to call a strike from unreported claims about wages, conditions or the response of an employer.",
     "Withholding labour is now the subject of a union's strike call. The event places the relationship between work and bargaining in public view. For {target}, responsibility should be judged without supplying a demand, a workplace closure or an agreement that this report does not establish.",
     "The colony has a call for strike action by a union. That is the known development; the course of the dispute is not specified here. An assessment of {target} should examine the politics of labour action without fabricating a turnout, a legal finding or a settlement."],
    ["The gazette records the call without presuming its subsequent course. A declared strike and an account of actual work stoppages are not interchangeable notices. The public record should also avoid attributing particular terms to the dispute where those terms have not been supplied as part of the reported event.",
     "Our movement believes a political principle should have something to say about the people who do the work. Collective action deserves serious judgment, including an examination of purpose and responsibility. Neither an instinctive cheer nor an instinctive denunciation is an adequate substitute for a principled position on labour relations.",
     "The right to act together matters because an individual worker need not have an equal voice in a bargain. A strike call should be considered with that imbalance in mind. Solidarity is a serious commitment, not a reason to invent either the demands or the outcome of this dispute.",
     "A strike call requires attention to labour relations without a fabricated estimate of lost output. Managers should distinguish the declaration from its practical extent and duration. A disciplined commercial view can take bargaining seriously while refusing to turn an unspecified action into a precise forecast of costs or interruption.",
     "A union has called a strike. That is the news, before somebody supplies a deserted factory, a furious owner or a perfect speech on a picket line. Working people and employers can be judged without that scenery. Keep the attention on the call and the responsibilities it raises."],
    ["The conduct of {target} should be examined against the strike call itself. This paper does not assign unreported demands or assume the participation and outcome of the labour action announced here.",
     "We criticise {target} in this dispute. Labour relations call for a responsible standard, and a strike call is an appropriate moment to question whether the interests at stake have been handled adequately.",
     "We support {target} in this assessment. A call for collective action deserves a fair account, and the existence of conflict does not establish that every accusation against a participant is justified."])

add("UNION_STRIKE_COLLAPSED",
    ["Strike collapses", "Labour action loses its course", "A strike ends in collapse"],
    ["A strike has collapsed in {colony}.", "The colony has seen a strike collapse.", "A strike in the colony has ended in collapse."],
    ["A strike has collapsed in {colony}. The collapse is a result for the labour action, not an established agreement about the underlying dispute. Readers judging {target} should avoid treating it as proof of a particular settlement, a change in wages or a complete account of responsibility.",
     "The course of a strike has reached collapse. That is serious news for the colony's labour relations, even without the reasons being specified. An assessment of {target} should distinguish the failure of the action from a judgment that every concern behind it has therefore been answered.",
     "A strike has ended in collapse in the colony. The report establishes that outcome without describing the circumstances that produced it. For {target}, the question is responsibility in the labour dispute, rather than an invented story about participation, concessions or the conduct of particular workers."],
    ["The gazette records the collapse without describing it as a negotiated settlement. The end of an action and the resolution of a dispute are distinct propositions. A reliable public notice should also avoid assigning a cause to the collapse where the particulars of that cause have not been supplied.",
     "A political movement should not confuse a failed action with a refutation of every principle associated with it. The proper argument concerns responsibility and purpose. Our convictions require attention to what a labour dispute means, rather than the convenience of treating its outcome as a complete moral judgment.",
     "Workers deserve solidarity in an unwelcome outcome as well as an attractive one. A strike's collapse does not make the needs of working people disappear. Labour should consider the action seriously without inventing either a betrayal or a bargain, and without making every worker answer for a result alone.",
     "The collapse of a strike is not a sufficient account of future labour conditions. Owners and managers should distinguish the action's outcome from the terms on which work may proceed. A commercial assessment requires actual arrangements rather than a presumption that collapse has settled every underlying issue in an employer's favour.",
     "The strike has collapsed. It is an ending, but do not turn it into a fairy tale in which every question has been solved. People can lose an action without losing the right to be heard. Readers deserve a plain account, not an invented villain to explain an unwelcome result."],
    ["The role of {target} merits examination without treating collapse as a full explanation. This paper records the outcome of the action while leaving unreported causes and terms outside the factual account.",
     "We judge {target} critically. A failed labour action is a proper occasion to ask whether responsibility has been exercised adequately, rather than to excuse poor judgment through the convenience of the outcome.",
     "We take a sympathetic view of {target}. Collapse does not prove every adverse claim about the people involved, and a fair hearing should survive an outcome that lends itself to easy recrimination."])

add("ECON_SOVEREIGN_DEFAULT",
    ["Government cannot pay its debts", "Public debt meets a payment failure", "The colony's government faces default"],
    ["The government of {colony} cannot pay its debts.", "The colony's government is unable to pay its debts.", "Government debt in the colony cannot be paid by the administration."],
    ["The colony's government cannot pay its debts. The inability to pay is the central financial fact, not an invitation to invent the amount owed. In assessing {target}, readers should distinguish this payment failure from unreported arrangements with creditors or a presumed cause of the government's position.",
     "A public promise to pay meets a hard limit when the government cannot honour its debts. That is the position reported in {colony}. Scrutiny of {target} should address the responsibility involved without supplying a creditor, an interest rate or a proposed remedy not established in the account.",
     "The government is unable to pay its debts. This is a statement about public finance with an immediate question of stewardship. For {target}, the relevant assessment should begin there, rather than with an invented account of bank failures, taxes or public services that the report does not describe."],
    ["The gazette records the government's inability to pay without specifying an unreported sum or creditor arrangement. Default and the measures taken in response are separate administrative facts. Public understanding requires care not to turn a financial condition into notice of a policy decision that has not been established.",
     "Public finance is political because obligations are made and honoured in the name of a common undertaking. Our principles require more than a clever explanation of a failure to pay. They require an argument about responsibility that does not lose the people of the colony behind the language of debt.",
     "Workers have reason to take public debts seriously without accepting that every burden belongs on their shoulders. Labour must ask who should answer for public financial stewardship. That question should not be confused with a claim that a particular wage or service has already been cut in response.",
     "An inability to pay is a credit event, but it is not a complete balance sheet. Business readers should avoid guessing the exposure of a creditor or the terms of a restructuring. The disciplined approach separates the known failure from a recovery calculation for which this report supplies no figures.",
     "The government cannot pay its debts. No fine wording will turn that into an account marked settled. It is a serious failure and a serious question about responsibility. Readers should not need a fictional bank panic or an invented unpaid bill to understand why public stewardship deserves attention."],
    ["The stewardship of {target} requires scrutiny against the inability to pay. This paper does not presume the origin of the debts or announce a response that the financial report has not established.",
     "We hold {target} to a critical standard. An inability to meet public debts is a fundamental failure of financial stewardship, and responsibility should not be displaced by an attractive description of the difficulty.",
     "We support {target} against an indiscriminate verdict. The failure to pay is serious, but it does not establish every accusation about its origins or prove that an imagined alternative would have performed better."])

add("ECON_SHIP_ARRIVED",
    ["Home-world ship reaches the colony", "An arrival on the colonial route", "The distant connection comes into port"],
    ["A ship from the home world has arrived in the colony.", "The colony has received the arrival of a home-world ship.", "A vessel from the home world has reached {colony}."],
    ["A ship from the home world has arrived in {colony}. The arrival is a concrete event in the colony's connection with its distant origin. Readers considering {target} should distinguish that fact from assumptions about particular goods, passengers or immediate changes in local supply not specified in this report.",
     "The distant route has produced an arrival: a ship from the home world has reached the colony. That is the established news, not a complete cargo account. For {target}, the relevant question is responsible attention to the connection without inventing what the vessel has brought or taken.",
     "A home-world vessel has arrived in the colony. Arrival and the practical disposition of a voyage's business are different subjects. An assessment of {target} should keep the known event clear, leaving unspecified freight, passenger figures and commercial outcomes outside the factual description of the ship's appearance."],
    ["The gazette records the arrival without presuming the contents of the vessel. A notice of a ship reaching the colony should not be enlarged into an account of deliveries or administrative arrangements not supplied here. The event has sufficient public significance without adding particulars to its official description.",
     "Our movement sees the home-world connection as a relationship between people as well as an item of transport. An arrival deserves attention to the common purposes that connection serves. A principled political account should keep those purposes visible without treating a vessel as proof that every local need is met.",
     "For workers, transport matters through the ordinary life it helps make possible. A ship's arrival should therefore be considered with people's needs in view. Labour has no reason to invent a cargo or a price change to make the point that the colony's connections are part of its common undertaking.",
     "An arrival is a logistics fact, not a completed account of supply and demand. Commercial readers should distinguish the vessel reaching the colony from delivery, settlement or the sale of particular goods. Sound planning requires the actual cargo and transaction record rather than an assumed benefit attached to the ship itself.",
     "A ship has arrived from the home world. A fine subject for attention, and no excuse to fill its hold with everything the imagination wants. Readers can take an interest in a distant connection without being promised a particular meal, purchase or reunion that this account does not establish."],
    ["The contribution of {target} should be examined through the reported arrival. This paper does not attribute an unspecified commercial or household consequence to the vessel's presence in the colony.",
     "We remain critical of {target}. An arrival should not place the stewardship of the colony's transport connection beyond scrutiny; the existence of a ship is not a complete account of responsible provision.",
     "We welcome {target} in this assessment. A tangible connection with the home world deserves recognition, while a fair account can acknowledge the arrival without pretending that every need has thereby been satisfied."])

add("PLANET_CYCLONE",
    ["Cyclone hits the colony", "A storm becomes the colony's news", "The colony faces a cyclone"],
    ["A cyclone has hit the colony.", "The colony has been struck by a cyclone.", "A cyclone has reached {colony}."],
    ["A cyclone has hit {colony}. The storm is established, but a particular loss or injury is not. Readers considering {target} should distinguish scrutiny of responsibility from blame for causing a natural event, and should not be asked to accept an invented damage total as part of the report.",
     "The colony has been struck by a cyclone. It is serious news without a fabricated account of its physical consequences. In assessing {target}, the relevant question concerns the responsibilities surrounding a storm, not an assumption that the weather itself proves a specific administrative or commercial failure.",
     "A cyclone is now part of the colony's experience. This report establishes the storm's occurrence, not a tally of damage. For {target}, scrutiny should address responsible conduct without supplying an evacuation, a rescue or a recovery that has not been established in the account of the event."],
    ["The gazette records the cyclone while withholding particulars of consequences not supplied to this notice. A natural event and the administrative response to it are distinct subjects. The public record should not attribute specific damage, casualties or measures to the storm on the strength of its occurrence alone.",
     "A political movement should be judged by its conception of common responsibility when nature is difficult. Our principles require attention to people and fair treatment, not an opportunity to turn weather into a convenient accusation. A serious position can demand responsibility without inventing either failure or heroism in response.",
     "Working people should remain at the centre of the question of safety. Labour's concern includes decent treatment when a natural event affects the colony's affairs. That is a reason for serious attention, not permission to announce injured workers or damaged homes that this report has not identified as facts.",
     "A cyclone is not a quantified loss statement. Owners and managers should distinguish the occurrence of a storm from specific effects on premises, output or credit. A prudent assessment can take the event seriously while refusing to attach an invented cost or duration of disruption to its name.",
     "A cyclone has hit. That is enough to command attention without a lurid scene supplied by imagination. Think about people. Think about responsibility. But do not let somebody sell a picture of ruined homes or injured neighbours as established news when the report contains no such account."],
    ["The conduct of {target} should be examined without treating the cyclone as proof of a particular response. This account records a natural event and avoids an unreported judgment of its physical consequences.",
     "We criticise {target} on the standard of stewardship surrounding this event. Weather is not a political choice, but responsibility should not disappear behind that fact or become immune from searching public scrutiny.",
     "We support {target} against easy blame. A cyclone is not evidence that every hostile claim about stewardship is true, and fair judgment must distinguish the natural event from the conduct being assessed."])

add("ECON_CONTRACT_SEVERELY_DELAYED",
    ["Building project badly behind schedule", "Construction timetable falls seriously short", "A project waits beyond its schedule"],
    ["A building project in the colony is badly behind schedule.", "Construction of a building project is severely delayed in {colony}.", "A colony building project has fallen badly behind its schedule."],
    ["A building project is badly behind schedule in {colony}. The delay is the established failure against its timetable, not a complete account of why it occurred. Readers considering {target} should distinguish that known position from invented shortages, contractor disputes or financial consequences not supplied in the report.",
     "A construction schedule is an expectation about when something will be ready. A building project in the colony is falling badly short of that expectation. In assessing {target}, the question is responsible delivery, without assuming either the cause of the delay or a new date for completion.",
     "The colony has a building project severely behind schedule. The gap between planned timing and delivery deserves scrutiny in its own right. For {target}, responsibility should be considered without attaching an unreported overrun, contractual penalty or abandoned purpose to the fact of the project's lateness."],
    ["The gazette records the serious delay without describing the project as cancelled or abandoned. Lateness and termination are different administrative conditions. The public record should also distinguish the reported position against schedule from any revised timetable, remedial instruction or explanation not established in the particulars supplied here.",
     "Promises about delivery belong within politics because public purposes require more than an intention on paper. Our movement should insist on responsibility for the distance between a plan and its execution. That principle does not require an invented account of who caused this particular project to fall behind.",
     "Workers know that a timetable can be treated as somebody else's promise and somebody else's problem. Labour should resist any account that makes ordinary people invisible in the question of delivery. A serious delay warrants attention without assuming that workers caused it or that speed should override decent conditions.",
     "A severe delay is a delivery issue, not automatically a quantified cost overrun. Managers should distinguish the schedule position from an assumed financial effect. Commercial scrutiny should concern the actual obligations and delivery record, without filling an incomplete account with a guessed penalty, cause or revised completion date.",
     "Behind schedule. Badly. A building project has failed the calendar's test, and there is no need to invent a row to make that interesting. Readers can demand responsibility without being promised a new finishing date that exists only because it makes the story feel more complete."],
    ["The stewardship of {target} warrants scrutiny against the severe delay. This report does not assign an unreported cause or presume that lateness means the project has been abandoned rather than delayed.",
     "We fault {target} over the standard of delivery. A schedule is not an ornament to a project, and serious lateness is a proper reason to question the adequacy of the stewardship involved.",
     "We defend {target} against a verdict based on the delay alone. Lateness is established, but its existence does not prove every adverse claim about responsibility or the merits of the project."])

add("COMP_LIQUIDATED",
    ["A company goes under", "Business failure enters the colony's record", "An enterprise reaches failure"],
    ["A company has gone under in {colony}.", "The colony has seen a company fail.", "A business in the colony has gone under."],
    ["A company has gone under in {colony}. The failure is a business event, not a detailed account of its consequences for particular people. Readers considering {target} should distinguish that known outcome from unreported claims about creditors, employment or the circumstances that brought the company to this position.",
     "A business has failed in the colony. An enterprise is more than a name in a commercial register, but its failure does not by itself identify every consequence. An assessment of {target} should address stewardship without supplying a balance sheet or a story about the firm's trade.",
     "The colony's business record includes a company going under. That outcome invites questions of responsibility without answering them all. For {target}, the relevant scrutiny should remain separate from an invented cause, a presumed creditor loss or an announcement about workers that the report does not establish."],
    ["The gazette records the company failure without describing an unreported distribution of assets or liabilities. The failure itself and subsequent legal or administrative arrangements require separate accounts. Precision is necessary where a commercial event could otherwise be enlarged into assumptions about individuals, public obligations or the course of proceedings.",
     "Our principles ask how an economy serves the colony, including when an enterprise fails. A business outcome should not make the people around it disappear into a convenient political slogan. Responsibility deserves an argument about stewardship, rather than a ready-made morality tale built from facts that are not known.",
     "Workers are not an incidental detail in the politics of business failure. Labour should keep ordinary lives in view without inventing a dismissal or an unpaid wage. Solidarity requires attention to people, and a careful account should not claim to know their particular circumstances merely because a company has gone under.",
     "A failed company is not a complete statement of creditor recoveries or wider commercial conditions. Owners and managers should distinguish the individual event from an economy-wide conclusion. A sound assessment requires the firm's actual position, rather than an assumed trade, a guessed debt or a forecast attached to failure alone.",
     "A company has gone under. A stark ending for an enterprise, and an invitation to a story with a villain already fitted. Resist the easy version. Readers can ask about responsibility without being handed an invented fortune, a stolen wage or a private quarrel as the explanation."],
    ["The responsibility of {target} should be examined without presuming the failure's cause. This paper records the business outcome while leaving unreported financial, employment and legal particulars outside its factual account.",
     "We judge {target} critically. Business failure deserves more than a shrug, and the standards of stewardship should be examined rather than dismissed as irrelevant once an enterprise has gone under.",
     "We take a sympathetic view of {target}. A failed enterprise does not establish every accusation of poor conduct, and fair assessment must survive an outcome that makes easy blame particularly tempting."])

add("ECON_LAYOFFS_MASS",
    ["Company lays off many workers", "A large loss of jobs at a company", "Workers face a company layoff"],
    ["A company has laid off many workers in {colony}.", "Many workers have been laid off by a company in the colony.", "The colony has seen a company carry out a large layoff."],
    ["A company has laid off many workers in {colony}. The scale is described as large, but a specific number is not supplied here. In assessing {target}, readers should distinguish the loss of jobs from an invented cause, severance arrangement or account of what will happen to those affected.",
     "Many workers have been laid off by a company. The event puts employment at the centre of the colony's business news. For {target}, the relevant scrutiny concerns responsibility towards people and the handling of work, without assuming either the company's trade or its financial reasons for the decision.",
     "A large layoff has taken place at a company in the colony. The loss of work deserves attention without an embellished account of individual households. Readers judging {target} should be able to consider the seriousness of the event without accepting unreported promises of new employment or support."],
    ["The gazette records the large layoff without assigning a count or a reason not supplied in the report. A reduction in employment and the failure of a company are distinct events. The account should not imply that the business has closed, or that a particular assistance arrangement has been established.",
     "Our politics should have something serious to say about people losing work. A principle that matters only when an economy is comfortable is a thin principle. The question of responsibility deserves attention without turning affected workers into scenery for an argument about a cause that has not been established.",
     "A layoff is about people whose work matters to their lives. Labour should begin there, with solidarity rather than an abstract admiration for flexibility. The report does not tell every household's story, and we should not invent one to make the case that workers deserve decent treatment when employment ends.",
     "A large layoff is an employment decision, not a complete financial statement. Commercial readers should avoid assuming a specific saving, a decline in demand or the closure of the enterprise. A useful assessment distinguishes the known decision from the business conditions and future results that would need their own evidence.",
     "Many people have lost their work at a company. That is the human centre of this story. It needs neither an invented tearful interview nor a convenient promise that everything will be fine. Readers can demand a serious standard of responsibility without being given a fictional household to feel for."],
    ["The conduct of {target} deserves scrutiny in relation to the layoff. This paper does not presume a financial cause, a compensation arrangement or the subsequent circumstances of those whose employment has been affected.",
     "We hold {target} to account critically. A large loss of jobs is not a minor adjustment in the lives of workers, and its stewardship deserves a more demanding standard than a convenient abstraction.",
     "We support {target} against a blanket adverse verdict. The layoff is serious, but the report does not establish every claim about its causes or prove that a particular imagined alternative was available."])

add("COMP_WORKPLACE_ACCIDENT",
    ["Accident at a workplace", "Workplace safety becomes immediate news", "An accident enters the working day"],
    ["An accident has occurred at a workplace in {colony}.", "The colony has had an accident at a workplace.", "A workplace in the colony has been the scene of an accident."],
    ["An accident has occurred at a workplace in {colony}. The occurrence is established, while a particular injury or legal finding is not supplied here. Readers considering {target} should distinguish scrutiny of safety responsibility from an invented account of the accident's cause or the condition of those involved.",
     "Safety is a practical concern before it is a subject for a statement. A workplace accident has occurred in the colony. An assessment of {target} should take that event seriously without presuming the kind of work, the number affected or a breach of rules not established by this account.",
     "The colony's news includes an accident at a workplace. That is sufficient reason for careful attention, not permission to imagine an injury or a rescue. For {target}, the relevant question is responsibility in the setting of work, with the known event kept distinct from its unreported particulars."],
    ["The gazette records the accident without announcing a legal conclusion. An occurrence at work and a finding of a breach are different matters. A sound public account should also avoid supplying an injury count or attributing a particular cause where those details have not been established in the report.",
     "Our convictions require that the conditions of work be treated as a public concern. Safety should not depend on how convenient it is to discuss. A serious political judgment can insist on responsibility while refusing to turn the occurrence of an accident into proof of particulars that have not been reported.",
     "Going to work should not make a person's safety an afterthought. Labour has every reason to insist on that principle. We should also distinguish an accident from an unreported finding about its cause, because solidarity requires a truthful account as well as a firm demand for decent conditions.",
     "A workplace accident warrants management attention without an invented estimate of liability or lost output. The event, its cause and any legal finding are distinct subjects. A disciplined assessment should take safety seriously while avoiding a financial calculation or an attribution of fault unsupported by the particulars supplied here.",
     "An accident at work. A plain statement, and a reason to remember that a workplace is full of people rather than merely output. No lurid description is needed. Readers deserve attention to safety without being sold an injury, a culprit or a scene that this report does not establish."],
    ["The role of {target} merits scrutiny against the accident. This paper does not presume a breach of rules or announce consequences for workers that have not been established in the reported particulars.",
     "We criticise {target} on the standard of safety stewardship. An accident warrants serious questions about responsibility, rather than a comfortable presumption that the conduct surrounding work should remain beyond public judgment.",
     "We defend {target} against automatic blame. The fact of an accident does not by itself establish a breach or settle responsibility, and a fair account should resist treating a feared explanation as proven."])

add("POL_GRANT_FAVOURITISM",
    ["Grant programme passes over needy districts", "Need goes unanswered in grant allocation", "Government grants miss the districts in need"],
    ["A government grant programme has passed over districts that needed it.", "Districts in need were passed over by a government grant programme.", "A government grant allocation has overlooked the districts that needed support."],
    ["A government grant programme has passed over districts that needed it. The allocation is a public stewardship question, not an invitation to invent the recipients. Readers considering {target} should distinguish the established failure to reach need from an unreported claim about a motive, a sum or a private favour.",
     "Need did not receive the attention it required in a government grant programme: districts that needed support were passed over. For {target}, the event raises a direct question about allocation. That question can be examined without adding a donor, an election bargain or a financial total to the account.",
     "The colony has a grant programme whose allocation passed over districts in need. That is the reported defect in public provision. An assessment of {target} should focus on the relationship between grants and need, rather than an invented explanation of why particular places were overlooked in the process."],
    ["The gazette records the omission of districts in need without supplying the programme's terms or a motive for its allocation. The distribution of grants deserves a clear administrative account. A statement about unmet need should not be enlarged into an unreported legal finding or a specific account of improper benefit.",
     "Our movement believes public provision should be judged by the purpose it is meant to serve. Need is not a decorative word for a programme's description. A political argument about grants should keep the overlooked districts at its centre rather than treating an allocation as virtuous simply because money was authorised.",
     "Labour's question is plain: whose need counts when public support is shared out? Districts in need should not vanish behind the language of a programme. Working people deserve allocation judged by its purpose, without an invented story about who personally benefited or what a particular household was denied.",
     "A grant programme should be assessed against its allocation objective, not merely the fact that it exists. Passing over districts in need is a significant defect against that measure. Commercial readers should distinguish that known problem from a guessed budget, a presumed recipient or an allegation about a private transaction.",
     "A grant programme, and the districts that needed it were passed over. The awkward part of the story is also the important part. No secret envelope is needed to make readers ask about fairness. Keep the attention on need, and on whether public provision is doing what it ought to do."],
    ["The stewardship of {target} requires examination against the districts passed over. This paper records the allocation problem without supplying an unreported intention, recipient or legal conclusion as its explanation.",
     "We judge {target} adversely. Public grants deserve an allocation that takes need seriously, and passing over the districts that needed support is a proper reason to question the fairness of stewardship.",
     "We support {target} against a wider verdict built on assumption. The allocation defect deserves attention, but it does not prove every accusation about motives or justify an invented account of private favour."])

add("POL_DEBATE_GAFFE",
    ["Party leader blunders in election debate", "A debate brings a leader's misstep", "Election argument meets an awkward moment"],
    ["A party leader has blundered in an election debate.", "An election debate has included a blunder by a party leader.", "A party leader has made a misstep in an election debate."],
    ["A party leader has blundered in an election debate. The misstep is established, but the words involved and their effect on voters are not supplied here. Readers assessing {target} should distinguish the debate event from a fabricated quotation or a claim that the election's outcome has been decided.",
     "An election debate has produced a leader's blunder. Public speaking is part of political leadership, though an awkward moment is not a complete political record. For {target}, the question is judgment under scrutiny, without inventing what was said or how the audience responded to the mistake.",
     "The colony's election argument includes a blunder by a party leader in debate. It is legitimate political news, not a substitute for the whole contest. An assessment of {target} should keep the misstep in proportion and leave polling changes or electoral consequences outside the factual account."],
    ["The gazette records the debate blunder without reproducing words not supplied to this notice. An error in a debate and a result at an election are distinct events. The report should not imply a measured change in support or attribute a particular response to the public without an adequate basis.",
     "A party's principles should be strong enough to be discussed beyond an awkward performance. That does not make a leader's judgment irrelevant. Our movement should distinguish the merits of conviction from the conduct of its public presentation, rather than allowing either a blunder or a clever recovery to settle everything.",
     "Workers deserve political debate about the conditions of their lives, not merely a competition in speaking neatly. A leader's blunder can deserve attention without displacing wages, safety and services from the argument. Labour should keep the standard practical and refuse to make a performance the whole measure of representation.",
     "A debate error is not an economic programme or an electoral result. Business readers should avoid pricing an imagined policy reversal into a speaking mistake. A sound assessment distinguishes communication, political judgment and actual decisions, rather than treating a blunder as a complete forecast of what a party would do.",
     "A leader has blundered in a debate. Tempting material for a perfect quotation, except the words are not supplied here. The mistake is news enough. Readers can judge a performance without being given an invented audience, a fictional blush or a claim that the whole election is suddenly over."],
    ["The performance of {target} deserves examination without assuming an electoral effect. This paper records the blunder and leaves the words involved and the public's response outside its factual account where they are unspecified.",
     "We criticise {target} in this assessment. Political leadership includes judgment under scrutiny, and a debate blunder is an appropriate occasion to question whether the standard of public presentation has been adequate.",
     "We defend {target} against an exaggerated verdict. A debate mistake does not erase the merits of a political position, and fairness requires more than turning an awkward moment into a complete judgment."])

add("ECON_FAMINE",
    ["Food shortage leaves the colony hungry", "Enough to eat remains the central need", "Hunger is a fact, not a figure of speech"],
    ["There is not enough food in {colony}, and people are going hungry.", "People in the colony are hungry because food is insufficient.", "The colony's food supply is insufficient, leaving people hungry."],
    ["People in {colony} are going hungry because there is not enough food. That is the central condition, without a cause or a timetable supplied here. Readers assessing {target} should distinguish the need for adequate provision from an invented account of how the shortage came about.",
     "Enough to eat is a basic requirement of daily life. The colony does not have enough food, and people are hungry. For {target}, the relevant scrutiny concerns the standard of provision, without assuming a particular policy failure or announcing a remedy not established by this report.",
     "The colony's food supply is insufficient and people are going hungry. A clear account should keep that practical condition in view. An assessment of {target} does not need an invented queue, a price increase or a crop failure to establish why adequate food deserves serious public attention."],
    ["The gazette records insufficient food and hunger as matters of public concern. A shortage and its explanation are distinct subjects, and the public record should not substitute an assumed cause for an established condition. Adequate provision remains the practical measure against which any response ought to be considered.",
     "Our principles should be intelligible to a person who needs a meal. Food belongs at the centre of politics because political life is supposed to concern the conditions in which people live. A serious position should be able to explain its purpose without losing the hungry person behind the argument.",
     "A wage matters because of the life it helps support. Food is among the most basic parts of that life, and labour should keep it in view. Solidarity begins with taking hunger seriously, without requiring a person to win a political argument before their need deserves public attention.",
     "An insufficient food supply is a basic economic constraint, not a complete account of its origins. Commercial readers should distinguish need from an assumed cause and an expression of confidence from actual provision. A practical assessment should return to whether people can obtain enough to eat, rather than admire an explanation.",
     "People are hungry. A plain fact with no need for an invented victim or a grand phrase. The colony can have all the arguments it likes about the future; the present still needs food. Readers should insist that the person who needs a meal remains the centre of this story."],
    ["The responsibility of {target} warrants attention without a verdict founded on an unreported cause. This paper records hunger as an established condition and keeps adequate provision at the centre of its account.",
     "We hold {target} to account critically. Hunger is an unacceptable condition for the colony, and the standard of stewardship should be judged against the basic requirement that people have enough to eat.",
     "We support {target} against an automatic adverse judgment. Hunger requires serious attention, but it does not establish every claim about its origin or prove that a particular imagined alternative would meet the need."])

